      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should `exit()` really reboot the system? `man exit` says `exit - cause normal process termination`.\n\nWhat should happen if `exit()` is called from dynamically spawned thread (Zephyr has support for them)?\n\nIf we want `exit()` to terminate non-essential threads, but panic on essential one, then `k_thread_abort()` looks like a perfect fit.",
